From b21e74165159319cc63fc30fbdc79edc89bcb77b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Certe Kim <18364439+CerteKim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:01:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_pas: allow forcing the TZMem SHM bridge

The PAS calls that load the metadata blob and that authenticate the firmware
memory region expect the firmware (hypervisor) to set up the SHM bridges on
behalf of Linux.  When Linux runs in EL2 there is no hypervisor left, and on
the Xiaomi Book S 12.4 (sc8180x) both calls then fail with -EINVAL:

  qcom_q6v5_pas 17300000.remoteproc: error -22 initializing firmware qcom/XIAOMI/BOOK124/qcadsp8180.mbn
  remoteproc remoteproc3: can't start rproc adsp: -22

while the same firmware loads fine at EL1.  qcom_scm_pas_prepare_and_auth_reset()
already implements the EL2 case (Linux creates the bridge itself), but
qcom_q6v5_pas only selects it for remotes that have an "iommus" property, which
it uses as the proxy for "Linux owns the memory protection".

Add a "qcom,needs-tzmem" bool so a platform can ask for it explicitly, which is
what an EL2 device tree overlay can do without inventing IOMMU stream IDs for a
remote that is not behind the SMMU.  qcom_tzmem_shm_bridge_create() returns
early when the SHM bridge is not in use, so the property is a no-op on EL1
trees, and the SHM bridge itself is only ever created in the self-owned form
(see "qcom,shm-bridge-vmid" and the tzmem EL2 change).

Signed-off-by: Certe Kim <18364439+CerteKim@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../bindings/remoteproc/qcom,pas-common.yaml  |  8 ++++++++
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c            | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,pas-common.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,pas-common.yaml
index 4607b45..df85dd2 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,pas-common.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/qcom,pas-common.yaml
@@ -55,6 +55,14 @@ properties:
     minItems: 1
     maxItems: 3
 
+  qcom,needs-tzmem:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      The PAS metadata blob and the firmware memory region have to be bridged
+      to the secure world by Linux itself, because the firmware that normally
+      creates these SHM bridges on behalf of Linux is not present (for example
+      when Linux runs in EL2 instead of under a hypervisor).
+
   qcom,smem-states:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle-array
     description: States used by the AP to signal the Hexagon core
diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
index 57dd279..e058717 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -737,6 +737,7 @@ static int qcom_pas_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct rproc *rproc;
 	const char *fw_name, *dtb_fw_name = NULL;
 	const struct rproc_ops *ops = &qcom_pas_ops;
+	bool needs_tzmem;
 	int ret;
 
 	desc = of_device_get_match_data(&pdev->dev);
@@ -850,8 +851,22 @@ static int qcom_pas_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		goto remove_ssr_sysmon;
 	}
 
-	pas->pas_ctx->use_tzmem = rproc->has_iommu;
-	pas->dtb_pas_ctx->use_tzmem = rproc->has_iommu;
+	/*
+	 * The PAS metadata blob and the firmware memory region have to be
+	 * bridged to the secure world.  Normally the firmware (hypervisor)
+	 * creates these SHM bridges on behalf of Linux, which is also why the
+	 * TZMem allocator must not be used in that case: passing a buffer that
+	 * is already part of an SHM bridge makes the PAS call fail.
+	 *
+	 * When Linux runs in EL2 there is no hypervisor left to do it, so the
+	 * bridges have to be created by Linux itself.  Platforms where this is
+	 * necessary (and where the SHM bridge is available) say so with
+	 * "qcom,needs-tzmem", usually from an EL2 device tree overlay.
+	 */
+	needs_tzmem = rproc->has_iommu ||
+		      device_property_read_bool(pas->dev, "qcom,needs-tzmem");
+	pas->pas_ctx->use_tzmem = needs_tzmem;
+	pas->dtb_pas_ctx->use_tzmem = needs_tzmem;
 	ret = rproc_add(rproc);
 	if (ret)
 		goto remove_ssr_sysmon;
-- 
2.56.0

